WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:07.639
Previously on Smallville, I always stuffs in the who has all my powers and none of my weaknesses.

00:00:07.639 --> 00:00:09.640
This can't be from your ship.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.640
But if this is still on Earth, so is the kryptonian that left it.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.640
As long as this rain remains on your finger and you have no power, destroy it.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.640
Kill!

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:25.019
I am your boss. I just bought The Daily Planet.

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:28.019
Clark, two weeks with no callback, what's going on?

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:31.019
My name is Julian Luther.

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:33.020
If he found out the truth, he could kill you.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.020
You think that this is Milton Fine?

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.020
It's the brain interactive construct.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.020
If any part of him was left behind to regenerate, then Fine could be outside.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.020
Clark, you're home.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.020
You have chosen to defy me.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.020
This defiance cannot go without consequence.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:01:32.689
I just want to remember this moment.

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:35.859
I should have.

00:01:35.859 --> 00:01:50.250
We should go somewhere.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:55.510
I'm happy right here.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.510
No, I mean we should leave Smallville.

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.760
We should go see the world, Bono.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.760
All the places you've ever tried.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.969
dreamed of.

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:06.969
How about Paris?

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:08.969
We'll have breakfast at the Anfield Tower.

00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:09.969
I am right.

00:02:09.969 --> 00:02:10.969
I'll fly you there myself.

00:02:10.969 --> 00:02:12.969
You have a lot of powers, Clark.

00:02:12.969 --> 00:02:15.969
But last I heard, flying wasn't one of them.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:21.169
You make me feel like I can fly.

00:02:21.169 --> 00:02:24.830
I'd better go.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:31.219
I have a meeting at the foundation.

00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:32.219
I tell you what?

00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:34.219
I'll make us a special dinner.

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:46.599
Our very own Paris.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.599
What a beautiful day.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:50.599
I almost forgot what the sun looked like.

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:51.599
The sun's got nothing on.

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:52.840
Son's got nothing on you.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.840
Why don't you close those curtains?

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:02.949
Come back to bed.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.430
I guess I could spare a few extra minutes.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:04:42.819
I love you, Clark Kent.

00:04:42.819 --> 00:04:43.819
Mr. Luther.

00:04:43.819 --> 00:04:48.629
If you've come to complain about my son's recent acquisition

00:04:48.629 --> 00:04:49.829
of your newspaper...

00:04:49.829 --> 00:04:51.230
This isn't about the paper.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.230
It's about something a little more personal.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.339
Paternity.

00:04:56.339 --> 00:05:00.110
You know, I've dealt with nuisances like this before,

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:05.920
but from the editor of the Daily Planet?

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:07.920
I'm already late for my meeting.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.800
I admit I'm not above embellishing a story,

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.399
but I couldn't

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.060
cook up something like this.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.019
What if I told you the only reason I'm standing here

00:05:16.019 --> 00:05:18.660
is because Lex Luther missed his baby brother?

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:37.899
Amazing, huh?

00:05:37.899 --> 00:05:42.100
Using DNA from the cord blood of your deceased son,

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:49.420
Lex created a carbon copy.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:50.959
Call me Julian.

00:05:50.959 --> 00:05:53.410
Dad.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.170
Lex warned me not to see you.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.689
He thinks I'm risking my life just standing here.

00:05:59.689 --> 00:06:01.850
But I'm in control of my life now,

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:07.209
and I plan to attack it head on.

00:06:07.209 --> 00:06:11.540
A courageous point of view.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.639
If you've got a problem with me,

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.860
Let's settle it right now.

00:06:15.459 --> 00:06:15.959
Problem.

00:06:19.149 --> 00:06:21.649
If you truly are my flesh and blood,

00:06:22.189 --> 00:06:28.279
get to know you, son.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.529
Hey, beautiful.

00:06:40.149 --> 00:06:42.600
What'd you find?

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.139
Another homeless man was murdered today.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.439
The seventh in the last two weeks.

00:06:51.199 --> 00:06:52.879
The police think it was a serial killer,

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.180
but I think we may have found the Kryptonian computer you mentioned.

00:06:57.579 --> 00:06:58.100
Brainiac.

00:07:00.459 --> 00:07:01.779
The brain interactive construct.

00:07:02.459 --> 00:07:03.480
Why do you think it's him?

00:07:04.019 --> 00:07:05.639
From the victim's coroner report.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.160
All of the bodies were found drained of their trace metals,

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.660
just like that technician from Lex's lab.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:17.680
Why do you think this thing is killing random people?

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.680
It must be regenerating,

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.680
using the trace metals from the human bodies.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.680
Clark, you have to stop it.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:29.819
The problem is if it doesn't want to be found,

00:07:29.819 --> 00:07:31.819
can literally disappear in the woodwork.

00:07:31.819 --> 00:07:33.819
I might be able to help with that.

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:39.939
All of the bodies were found randomly scattered

00:07:39.939 --> 00:07:40.939
across the distance.

00:07:40.939 --> 00:07:46.939
across the district so I triangulated the attacks to find a possible home base.

00:07:46.939 --> 00:07:48.939
Suicide slums.

00:07:48.939 --> 00:07:50.939
I'm impressed.

00:07:50.939 --> 00:07:55.660
Chloe's not the only one who knows her way around a computer now.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:08:00.040
What would I do without you?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:50.340
You've fallen far from your ivory tower.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.340
Haven't you, Professor?

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:58.529
You're not Cal L.

00:08:58.529 --> 00:09:01.529
I'm the new and improved version.

00:09:01.529 --> 00:09:04.529
Don't fool yourself.

00:09:04.529 --> 00:09:05.529
Phantom.

00:09:05.529 --> 00:09:11.529
You're nothing more than a failed lab experiment dressed up in a Kryptonian's body.

00:09:11.529 --> 00:09:14.529
Where is the Boy Scout?

00:09:14.529 --> 00:09:16.529
I'm not sure.

00:09:16.529 --> 00:09:18.529
These Martian friends took me prisoner.

00:09:18.529 --> 00:09:20.529
But I managed to escape.

00:09:20.529 --> 00:09:22.529
When I got back, Kent was gone.

00:09:22.529 --> 00:09:26.529
So I thought I'd step into his shoes.

00:09:26.529 --> 00:09:28.529
You know what? They fit perfectly.

00:09:28.529 --> 00:09:34.529
Aren't you concerned how Calell will react when he comes home to find you in bed with his girlfriend?

00:09:34.529 --> 00:09:37.529
If Kent was alive, he'd be back by now.

00:09:37.529 --> 00:09:40.529
Trust me, he's long gone.

00:09:40.529 --> 00:09:43.529
Well, lucky you.

00:09:43.529 --> 00:09:45.529
Oh.

00:09:45.529 --> 00:09:46.529
There is one problem.

00:09:46.529 --> 00:09:49.529
The yellow sun, it turns my skin to stone.

00:09:49.529 --> 00:09:52.529
It's only a matter of time before someone figures out that I'm not, Ken.

00:09:52.529 --> 00:09:55.529
I know how smart you are, I thought you could help.

00:09:55.529 --> 00:09:58.529
Try a good sunscreen.

00:09:58.529 --> 00:10:00.529
Wide-brimmed half, perhaps.

00:10:00.529 --> 00:10:02.529
Can't allow me.

00:10:02.529 --> 00:10:03.529
They have destroyed you.

00:10:03.529 --> 00:10:04.529
Help me.

00:10:04.529 --> 00:10:06.529
I promise?

00:10:06.529 --> 00:10:08.529
I'll finish the job.

00:10:08.529 --> 00:10:11.529
I'm in no condition to help you.

00:10:11.529 --> 00:10:14.529
But there is someone.

00:10:14.529 --> 00:10:20.370
A Kryptonian.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:24.370
He came to Earth years ago and stayed.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:26.370
His name is Daxoer.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:28.370
One of Krypton's greatest scientist.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.370
He'll know how to fix you.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:34.220
How can I find him?

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.220
Well, and Kryptonians travel through a portal.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:39.220
They carried a beacon so they could be located.

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:40.200
Small.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:44.220
shield-shaped device, synchronized to their individual genetic code.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.220
Daxoers fell in the human hands.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.220
Find it, and you'll find him.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:52.220
Are you, uh...

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:54.220
Are you, uh, are you telling me the truth?

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:56.220
Lying to you would be like lying to a mollusk.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.220
There's no point.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:04.330
This doesn't check out.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.330
I'll shove you back into the test tube myself.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:23.730
It's like some people lost the jobs.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.730
Casualties of the new commander-in-chief, Lex Luthor.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:30.730
Luther. Out with the old, in with the new, and easily controlled.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:31.730
What's up?

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:32.730
I need you to help me find someone.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:33.730
Cryptonian scientist.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.730
Another Kryptonian?

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:36.730
Jeez, Clark.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:40.730
I'm starting to think that Earth was your home planet's top tourist destination.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:41.730
How's you hear about this guy?

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:43.730
Jarrell told me.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:45.730
Look, Clark, usually I'm right there to help,

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.730
but right now my hands are so full.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:51.730
And, uh, no offense, but cryptonians aren't exactly low maintenance.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.730
The only way I'm going to find this guy is to hunt on the tracking device.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:55.730
There's a rumor that some people found it.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.730
I thought the planet's archive might show a record.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:11:59.730
Clark, look around.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.730
Lex launched a torpedo through the hull of the Daily Planet,

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:05.730
and I'm just barely hanging onto the lifeboat.

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:06.730
Can't this wait?

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.730
It will only take a second, Chloe.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.730
As soon as I find out who has this shield, I'll be out of your hair.

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:12.730
Shield?

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:15.730
Don't you already have one of those?

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.600
The Kryptonian SOS from the Time Capsule, remember a beauty pageant,

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.600
gorgeous gold diggers?

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:32.389
Yeah.

00:12:32.389 --> 00:12:35.830
Clark, why don't you go home and just take a breather, and I'll call you?

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:37.830
and I'll call you later.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:39.830
Where is it, Coy?

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:49.740
I just really need to find it.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.740
I was hoping you could jog my memory.

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:56.039
You never forget anything.

00:12:56.039 --> 00:12:59.039
Mine's like a titanium trap.

00:12:59.039 --> 00:13:03.039
Look, do you remember where I put the shield or not?

00:13:03.039 --> 00:13:06.639
I'm sorry, Clark, I can't help you.

00:13:06.639 --> 00:13:25.110
Dreeze. Lex, what is so damn important you had to pull me out of a crucial negotiation?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:30.110
Well, according to the Luther Court visitor's law, Grant Gabriel came to see you yesterday.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:34.110
He did, yes.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:39.110
To discuss one of your latest projects, Mr. Gabriel, is at the center of it.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:42.110
You've always shun newspapers, Dad.

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:45.110
You used to tell me they're nothing but lies delivered daily.

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:48.110
I may have underestimated the power of the media.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:52.110
And I was curious about your trusted lieutenant.

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:55.110
Then what'd you think of him?

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:58.110
Insightful. Courageous?

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.110
Direct.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.110
Direct.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.110
Your exact opposite, Lex.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:06.110
Yeah, well, keep your distance.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.110
I'll deal with Grant myself from now on.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.110
You say that as if he belongs to you.

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:15.970
Grant Gabriel is an adult.

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:18.970
You may be his employer, but...

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:22.970
You can't claim him as if he were a piece of property.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:31.139
You know, don't you?

00:14:31.139 --> 00:14:34.139
Do you believe you have the right to recycle your dead brother

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:37.139
as if he were part of some sick vanity project?

00:14:37.139 --> 00:14:38.139
Well, I only did what you were.

00:14:38.139 --> 00:14:39.639
You never had the guts to do.

00:14:39.639 --> 00:14:41.639
What you've done is depraved.

00:14:41.639 --> 00:14:45.210
You disgust me.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.710
You're telling me you wouldn't want to see Julian again.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:51.879
Into the eyes of the sun you lost.

00:14:51.879 --> 00:15:28.220
Lana.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:30.220
Chloe, what are you doing here?

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.220
I was actually looking for Clark.

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:35.220
He came by the Daily Planet and he was acting beyond weird.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:38.220
Have you noticed anything different about him recently?

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.220
Yeah, I have.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:44.700
He's finally opened up and let me in.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.700
Chloe, he's more understanding.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:50.940
he's more understanding than ever.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:54.940
Lana, he insisted that I help him find a Kryptonian shield

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.940
that he already has.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:59.940
The clerk I know would never forget something like that.

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:02.940
Well, maybe you don't know him as well as you think.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.940
After everything he's been through, I think he's just taking some time

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.940
to focus on his own happiness.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:12.860
His priorities are different.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:16.860
Well, his priorities may be different,

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:19.860
but his personality is in a whole other universe.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:24.860
Lana, I've been a part of Clark's inner circle for a while now.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:26.860
I know when he's not himself.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:31.860
Chloe, maybe it's time for you to let go of him a little.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:35.679
I'm not hanging on.

00:16:35.679 --> 00:16:37.679
There's something wrong with him.

00:16:37.679 --> 00:16:42.909
Hey, Chloe, you seem a little tense.

00:16:42.909 --> 00:16:48.529
Did you tell about the move?

00:16:48.529 --> 00:16:51.580
What move?

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:57.899
I wasn't going to say anything until it was official.

00:16:57.899 --> 00:17:00.899
But after Lana and I type a few loose ends,

00:17:00.899 --> 00:17:02.899
or leaving Smallville.

00:17:02.899 --> 00:17:04.900
together.

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:23.619
To say. Actually, I think I should just go.

00:17:23.619 --> 00:17:33.099
Is she okay?

00:17:33.099 --> 00:17:36.099
She thinks that there's something wrong with you.

00:17:36.099 --> 00:17:38.099
She says that you went to see her

00:17:38.099 --> 00:17:42.099
and you completely forgot about this Kryptonian shield that you have?

00:17:42.099 --> 00:17:45.099
I didn't forget anything. I just can't find it anymore.

00:17:45.099 --> 00:17:48.480
I think Kara might have taken it.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:53.559
If it's Kryptonian, do you think that she brought it up to the fortress?

00:17:53.559 --> 00:18:27.180
I'm searching for something.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.180
I think Kara may have brought it here.

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:31.180
brought it here.

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:36.700
Leave here at once, Phantom.

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:42.539
And what if I don't?

00:18:42.539 --> 00:18:43.539
It's just a voice, Dorelle.

00:18:43.539 --> 00:18:45.539
An echo from the past.

00:18:45.539 --> 00:18:48.539
Me, what are you going to do?

00:18:48.539 --> 00:18:50.539
Next to meet him?

00:18:50.539 --> 00:18:53.539
You are not welcome here.

00:18:53.539 --> 00:18:55.539
Don't worry, Jurel.

00:18:55.539 --> 00:18:59.369
I'll find it sooner or later.

00:18:59.369 --> 00:19:15.230
The last Phantom has returned, Carlis.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:20.279
You must defeat him.

00:19:20.279 --> 00:19:41.059
Lada!

00:19:41.059 --> 00:19:42.059
Clark, what is it?

00:19:42.059 --> 00:19:43.059
I'm right here.

00:19:43.059 --> 00:19:45.440
God, you're okay.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:48.440
Of course I'm okay.

00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:51.940
You've only been gone an hour.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:56.119
Lana, I've been gone for weeks.

00:19:56.119 --> 00:19:58.119
Clark, I know that time's different in the fortress,

00:19:58.119 --> 00:20:00.119
but check the clock.

00:20:00.119 --> 00:20:02.119
You just saw me before you went up there to find the shield.

00:20:02.119 --> 00:20:04.119
No, Lana, that wasn't me.

00:20:04.119 --> 00:20:07.500
It was the Phantom.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:09.500
Lana, he looks exactly like me.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.970
Joel trapped me in the fortress.

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:14.970
He released me to stop the Phantom.

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:17.970
No, I'm sure it was you.

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:18.970
Clark, it had to be.

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:20.970
to be.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.970
Chloe said that you've been having troubles with your memory.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.970
Just think, Clark.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:29.970
Remember in bed when you said you were going to fly me to Paris.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:36.099
We were going to leave Smallville together.

00:20:36.099 --> 00:20:48.140
I'm sorry.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:50.140
This is all my fault.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.140
I need to get you out here.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:52.140
There's not much time.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:54.140
He can be back any second.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:21:01.599
Change a plan.

00:21:01.599 --> 00:21:03.599
We have a problem.

00:21:03.599 --> 00:21:05.599
