How many times have you been married now, anyway?

00:37:50.230 --> 00:37:52.230
You ungrateful, son of the bitch.

00:37:52.230 --> 00:37:55.230
If it wasn't for me, you'd still be a smudge in a petri dish.

00:37:55.230 --> 00:37:57.230
Yeah, you're some genius.

00:37:57.230 --> 00:38:00.230
You're so lonely and pathetic you had to build yourself a brother.

00:38:00.230 --> 00:38:02.230
I gave you everything!

00:38:02.230 --> 00:38:04.230
You turned your back on me.

00:38:04.230 --> 00:38:07.230
on me, you throw it all the way.

00:38:07.230 --> 00:38:10.230
I'm not throwing anything away.

00:38:10.230 --> 00:38:13.230
Go ahead, kick me out of my office.

00:38:13.230 --> 00:38:17.230
It gives me more time to enjoy the full benefits of being a Luther.

00:38:17.230 --> 00:38:33.900
Last I heard, I was practically made for this family.

00:38:33.900 --> 00:38:36.900
There's nothing like a good New York sirloin.

00:38:36.900 --> 00:38:43.900
Dry aged for 35 days and enjoyed over two glorious hours.

00:38:43.900 --> 00:38:44.900
Thanks, Lion.

00:38:44.900 --> 00:38:45.900
Yeah, well, after a little,

00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:49.900
Well, after a good dinner, one can forgive anybody,

00:38:49.900 --> 00:38:51.900
even one's own relations.

